Article 12. The People's Court shall accept the following lawsuits brought by citizens, legal persons or other organizations:
(1) Those objecting to administrative penalties such as administrative detention, suspension or revocation of permits and licenses, an order for suspension of production and business, confiscation of illegal gains, confiscation of illegal property, fines, or warnings;
(2) Those objecting to administrative compulsory measures such as restrictions on personal freedom or sealing up, seizure, or freezing of property, or to administrative compulsory enforcement;
(3) Those applying for administrative licenses, where the administrative organ refuses to respond or fails to respond within the statutory time limit, or objecting to other decisions made by the administrative organ concerning administrative licenses;
(4) Those objecting to decisions made by administrative organs concerning the confirmation of ownership or right to use of natural resources such as land, mineral deposits, water bodies, forests, mountains, grasslands, wasteland, tidal flats, and sea areas;
(5) Those objecting to expropriation or requisition decisions and the related compensation decisions;
(6) Those applying to administrative organs to perform statutory duties to protect personal rights, property rights, and other lawful rights and interests, where the administrative organ refuses to perform or fails to respond;
(7) Those considering that administrative organs have infringed upon their rights to autonomous management or rights to rural land contractual management or rural land management rights;
(8) Those considering that administrative organs have abused administrative power to exclude or restrict competition;
(9) Those considering that administrative organs have illegally raised funds, apportioned expenses, or illegally demanded performance of other obligations;
(10) Those considering that administrative organs have not paid pensions, minimum living security benefits, or social insurance benefits in accordance with the law;
(11) Those considering that administrative organs have failed to perform in accordance with the law, performed not in accordance with the agreement, or illegally changed or terminated government concession agreements, land and housing expropriation compensation agreements, or other agreements;
(12) Those considering that administrative organs have infringed upon other personal rights, property rights, or other lawful rights and interests.
In addition to the provisions of the preceding paragraph, the People's Court shall accept other administrative cases that may be brought to court as provided for by laws and regulations.

Article 13. The People's Court shall not accept lawsuits brought by citizens, legal persons or other organizations concerning the following matters:
(1) State acts such as national defense and foreign affairs;
(2) Administrative regulations, rules, or decisions and orders with general binding force formulated and issued by administrative organs;
(3) Decisions of administrative organs on rewards and punishments, appointments and removals of their staff;
(4) Administrative acts that are finally decided by administrative organs as provided for by law.

Article 15. The Intermediate People's Court shall have jurisdiction over the following first-instance administrative cases:
(1) Cases brought against administrative acts performed by departments under the State Council or by local people's governments at or above the county level;
(2) Cases handled by customs;
(3) Major and complex cases within its jurisdiction;
(4) Other cases that shall be under the jurisdiction of the Intermediate People's Court as provided for by law.

Article 31. A party or legal representative may entrust one or two persons as litigation agents.
The following persons may be entrusted as litigation agents:
(1) lawyers and basic-level legal service workers;
(2) close relatives or staff members of the party;
(3) citizens recommended by the community, unit, or relevant social organization to which the party belongs.

Article 33. Evidence shall include:
(1) documentary evidence;
(2) physical evidence;
(3) audio-visual materials;
(4) electronic data;
(5) testimony of witnesses;
(6) statements of the parties;
(7) expert evaluation opinions;
(8) records of inspection and records of the scene.
The above evidence may serve as the basis for determining the facts of a case only after being verified as true by the court.

Article 41: Where the plaintiff or a third party cannot collect the following evidence related to this case on its own, it may apply to the People's Court for obtaining the evidence:
(1) Evidence kept by a state organ which must be obtained by the People's Court;
(2) Evidence involving state secrets, trade secrets or personal privacy;
(3) Other evidence that genuinely cannot be collected on its own due to objective reasons.

Article 49: The institution of an action shall meet the following conditions:
(1) The plaintiff is a citizen, legal person or any other organization that meets the requirements of Article 25 of this Law;
(2) There is a clear defendant;
(3) There is a specific claim and factual basis; and
(4) The case falls within the scope of acceptance of the People's Court and the jurisdiction of the People's Court accepting the case.

Article 56: During the litigation, enforcement of the administrative act shall not be suspended. However, an adjudication to suspend enforcement shall be made under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The defendant considers that suspension of enforcement is necessary;
(2) The plaintiff or an interested person applies for suspension of enforcement, and the People's Court considers that enforcement of the administrative act will cause irreparable damage and that suspension of enforcement will not harm national interests or public interests;
(3) The People's Court considers that enforcement of the administrative act will cause major harm to national interests or public interests;
(4) Laws or regulations provide for suspension of enforcement.
If a party is not satisfied with an adjudication to suspend or not to suspend enforcement, the party may apply for one reconsideration.

Article 59: Where a participant in the litigation or any other person commits any of the following acts, the People's Court may, depending on the circumstances and seriousness of the act, admonish the person, order the person to make a statement of repentance, or impose a fine of not more than 10,000 yuan or detention of not more than 15 days; if a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) Where a person who is obligated to assist in investigation or enforcement, without justified reasons, procrastinates, refuses, or obstructs investigation or enforcement with respect to a decision of a People's Court to assist in investigation or a notice of a People's Court to assist in enforcement;
(2) Forging, concealing, destroying evidence or providing false evidentiary materials, obstructing the People's Court from adjudicating the case;
(3) Instigating, suborning by offering money, or coercing others to give false testimony, or threatening or preventing witnesses from testifying;
(4) Concealing, transferring, selling, or damaging property that has been sealed up, seized, or frozen;
(5) Using illegal means such as deception or coercion to cause the plaintiff to withdraw the complaint;
(6) Using violence, threats, or other methods to obstruct judicial officers of a People's Court from performing their duties, or disturbing the work order of the People's Court by making noise, storming the court, or by other means;
(7) Intimidating, insulting, slandering, framing, assaulting, besieging, or retaliating against judicial officers or other staff of the People's Court, participants in litigation, or persons assisting in investigation or enforcement.
Where a unit commits any of the acts prescribed in the preceding paragraph, the People's Court may impose a fine or detention on the person in charge of the unit or the person directly responsible in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph; if a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law.
A fine or detention must be approved by the president of the People's Court. If a party is not satisfied, the party may apply for one reconsideration to the People's Court at the next higher level. During the reconsideration period, enforcement shall not be suspended.

Article 70: If an administrative act falls under any of the following circumstances, the People's Court shall render a judgment to annul or partially annul it, and may render a judgment ordering the defendant to perform a new administrative act:
(1) Insufficiency of main evidence;
(2) Incorrect application of laws or regulations;
(3) Violation of legal procedures;
(4) Exceeding authority;
(5) Abuse of authority;
(6) Manifestly improper.

Article 74 Where an administrative act falls under any of the following circumstances, the People's Court shall render a judgment confirming the illegality but shall not revoke the administrative act:
(1) the administrative act shall be revoked according to law, but revocation would cause significant harm to national interests or public interests;
(2) the procedure of the administrative act is slightly illegal but does not have a practical impact on the rights of the plaintiff.
Where an administrative act falls under any of the following circumstances and does not need to be revoked or a judgment of performance rendered, the People's Court shall render a judgment confirming the illegality:
(1) the administrative act is illegal but has no content that can be revoked;
(2) the defendant has changed the original illegal administrative act, but the plaintiff still requests confirmation that the original administrative act is illegal;
(3) the defendant fails to perform or delays performance of statutory duties, and a judgment of performance would be meaningless.

Article 82 When hearing the following first-instance administrative cases, if the People's Court finds the facts clear, the rights and obligations clear, and the dispute minor, it may apply summary procedure:
(1) the alleged administrative act was made on the spot according to law;
(2) the case involves an amount of money not exceeding 2,000 yuan;
(3) the case falls under a government information disclosure case.
For first-instance administrative cases other than those specified in the preceding paragraph, if all parties agree to the application of summary procedure, summary procedure may be applied.
Summary procedure shall not apply to cases remanded for retrial or retried under the trial supervision procedure.

Article 89 When hearing an appeal case, the People's Court shall handle it respectively according to the following circumstances:
(1) if the facts are clearly found and the laws and regulations are correctly applied in the original judgment or ruling, the appeal shall be dismissed and the original judgment or ruling affirmed by judgment or ruling;
(2) if the findings of facts are erroneous or the laws and regulations are incorrectly applied in the original judgment or ruling, the judgment or ruling shall be modified, revoked, or changed according to law;
(3) if the basic facts are unclear or the evidence is insufficient in the original judgment, the case shall be remanded to the original trial People's Court for retrial, or the judgment shall be modified after the facts are clarified;
(4) if there are serious violations of legal procedures such as omission of a party or illegal default judgment in the original judgment, the original judgment shall be revoked by ruling and the case remanded to the original trial People's Court for retrial.
If a party files an appeal after the original trial People's Court renders a judgment on a case remanded for retrial, the second instance People's Court shall not remand the case for retrial again.
If the People's Court needs to change the original judgment when hearing an appeal case, it shall at the same time render a judgment on the alleged administrative act.

Article 91 Where a party's application falls under any of the following circumstances, the People's Court shall conduct a retrial:
(1) there is definite error in the decision not to docket the case or to dismiss the prosecution;
(2) there is new evidence sufficient to overturn the original judgment or ruling;
(3) the main evidence for finding the facts in the original judgment or ruling is insufficient, was not cross-examined, or is forged;
(4) the application of laws or regulations in the original judgment or ruling is definitely erroneous;
(5) there is a violation of the legally-prescribed litigation procedure that may affect a fair trial;
(6) the original judgment or ruling omits a claim;
(7) the legal document on the basis of which the original judgment or ruling was made has been revoked or changed;
(8) the trial personnel engaged in acts such as corruption, bribery, favoritism, or perverting the law when trying the case.

Article 96: Where an administrative organ refuses to perform a judgment, ruling or mediation document, the first-instance People's Court may take the following measures:
(1) For a fine that shall be returned or a sum that shall be paid, notify the bank to transfer the amount from the account of the administrative organ;
(2) Where the administrative organ fails to perform within the prescribed time limit, impose a fine of fifty to one hundred yuan per day on the person in charge of the administrative organ, calculated from the date of expiration of the time limit;
(3) Publicly announce the refusal of the administrative organ to perform;
(4) Submit a judicial recommendation to the supervisory organ or the administrative organ at the next higher level. The organ that receives the judicial recommendation shall handle the matter in accordance with the relevant provisions and inform the People's Court of the handling result;
(5) Where the administrative organ refuses to perform the judgment, ruling or mediation document and the social impact is severe, may detain the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible persons of the administrative organ; if the circumstances are so serious as to constitute a crime, investigate criminal liability according to law.
